Fictional Band Name: Mercury Consort

Band Description: Mercury Consort is a five-member chamber-drive ensemble built around the principle that rhythmic constancy can make contrapuntal complexity feel more physical rather than more academic.

Elena Vogt — treble viola da gamba, primary motif design, upper suspensions, register crossings.
Tobias Rehm — tenor and bass viola da gamba, low ostinati, pedal tones, imitative entries.
Lukas Kern — dry motorik drums, pulse continuity, minimal orchestration shifts.
Miriam Schade — prepared clavinet, muted repetition, metallic harmonic punctuation.
Jonas Frei — bass clarinet, chalumeau pedals, breath texture, transitional low register.

There is no conventional frontperson. Lukas establishes an almost immovable temporal floor while Elena and Tobias create internal movement through counterpoint. Miriam supplies mechanical articulation, and Jonas temporarily thickens the harmonic underside before withdrawing. Live pieces can extend substantially because the group changes voice relationships instead of changing groove.

